---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Save a board or a part of it as a template.
The objects are converted to the web app's format and a thumbnail drawn by holst is uploaded. It prints the new template with its id.

USAGE
  holst template create <board> <name> [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to take the objects from
  name    The template's name

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws       The workspace a new thing goes to: id or part of its name; needed when you have several
      --description text   The template's description; none by default
      --for who            Who can use it: me or workspace; me by default
      --frame frame        An area as a frame: id, link, title or part of a title
      --object object      An object, repeat for several: id, link, @N or the first 8 characters of its id
  -n, --dry-run            Show what would change; change nothing

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst tpl create "Roadmap" "Quarter plan" --for workspace
  $ holst tpl create "Roadmap" "Q3 frame" --frame "Q3"

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
